  "query_preview": "..\n(Tomorrow through Tuesday)\nIssued at 1151 AM CDT Tue Aug 11 2026\n\nFor the remainder of the work week, near persistent daily\nconditions will be in the offing, with upper level high pressure\nsolidly in control of the weather across the area through at \nleast the weekend and likely into next week as well. Low level\ntemperatures support continued widespread triple digit ambient\ntemperatures across the region, with heat index values mainly in \nthe 105 to 110 range. Overnight low temperatures are also expected\nto remain similar, providing little relief from the afternoon\nheat. The aforementioned extension of the Heat Advisory through\nthe day Friday was a fairly conservative one, and the expectation\nis that this will need to eventually be extended through at least\nthe weekend. Uncertainty increases slightly for the early part of\nnext week, with the high pressure center shifting westward and\npotential for a disturbance and weak cool front to affect mainly\nnorthern portions of the region. The bulk of the impacts from this\nstill look to remain north of the area but these features may\nbring a modest uptick in the rain chances for a lucky few.",
